---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
---

<Page title="Blogs">
    <h1>
        Blogs
    </h1>
    <p class="description">
        Articles, rants, and shitposts - free of AI slop
    </p>

    <div class="post">
        <div class="post-info">
            <h2>My thoughts on AI</h2>
            <p class="date">Posted on 2026-11-25</p>
            <p>
                In the past couple of years, AI went from "there are 2 Rs in 'strawberry'"
                to becoming a tool that most programmers frequently use to debug or write
                code. It is no doubt that such a change is a substantial one, and that it
                happened in a few short years, during which, lots of people developed
                reliance on their AI models, unable to write a simple for loop on their own 
                anymore.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
            <a href="/blogs/my-thoughts-on-ai">Read more↗</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="post">
        <div class="post-info">
            <h2>Chess, and programming</h2>
            <p class="date">Posted on 2026-11-25</p>
            <p>
                Elon Musk recently had a funny encounter with chess.com, when he proposed the 
                possiblity that chess could one day be solved. This take, IMO, shows ignorance 
                on the subject on his part, and in this article, I will try to discuss chess,
                its relevance in programming, and why I think although computers can pretend
                to play chess perfectly, it willl never be fully solved.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="links">
            <a href="/blogs/">Read more↗</a>
        </div>
    </div>

</Page>

<style>

    .description {
        color: var(--color-mute);
        font-style: italic;
        text-align: center;
        padding-bottom: 2rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mute);
    }

    .post {
        margin: 1rem;
        padding: 1rem 3rem 2rem;
        
        border: var(--color-mute) 1px solid;
        border-radius: 10px;
    }

    .post h2 {
        margin-bottom: 8px;
    }

    .date {
        font-style: italic;
        color: var(--color-mute);
    }
</style>
